[1;38;2;25;103;210m  ## Wrong assumptions / gaps[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  [m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  1. **The task is already satisfied, and the plan does not confront that.**[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  `README.md` was added in commit `2e184e1` and already documents all five[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  commands and all three agents in detail; the working tree even has a further[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  uncommitted edit adding the "Stage Completion Signal" section (`git diff[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  README.md` shows +3 lines). The plan's step 1 is an "audit and finalize" with[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  **no stated concrete change**. Because the task literally reads "Add a simple[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  README.md", the plan must decide and declare one of:[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m     - the existing README already satisfies the task (documentation-only,[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  minimal or zero edits), or[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m     - the specific edits/corrections to make (see item 2).[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m     Without this, the implementation stage has undefined output, and the[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  downstream implementation-review stage may reject a zero-diff result even[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  though the requirement is met.[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  [m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  2. **The plan lists "verify" items but silently leaves two known inaccuracies[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  uncorrected.** These are the only real edits the task likely needs:[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m     - **Go version:** README says "Go 1.25+" but `go.mod`'s `go 1.25.6`[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  directive means **at least 1.25.6**. Should read `1.25.6+`.[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m     - **Artifacts example is misleading:** README shows `3-implement.md (or[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  3-fix.md on subsequent cycles)`. `builder.artifactPath` increments a single[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  counter, so a cycle-2 fix is actually `5-fix.md` with `6-review.md`, not[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  `3-fix.md`. The example tree should reflect the real sequential numbering (or[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  drop the parenthetical).[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  [m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  3. **The plan's own verification step 2 is unsound.** `git diff --stat --[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  '*.go'` already reports five modified Go files from pre-existing work.[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  Running it after the implementation stage will *always* show Go changes, so[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  it cannot distinguish "README task touched Go" from "Go was already dirty".[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  Replace with a before/after comparison — e.g. record `git diff -- '*.go' |[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  shasum` (or the mtimes) at the start of the implementation stage and assert[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  it is unchanged at the end; or simply assert that `git status --porcelain`[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  shows **no new** Go paths relative to the baseline.[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  [m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  4. **"Simple README" vs. the existing ~140-line document is unresolved.** The[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  task asks for a *simple* README; the current file is thorough. The plan[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  should state explicitly that coverage/accuracy wins over brevity and that the[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  existing structure is kept, otherwise the implementation or review stage may[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  argue for trimming content the task actually requires.[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  [m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  5. **No acceptance criterion tied to the task wording.** The plan front-loads[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  exit codes, build workflow, and artifact layout. It should separate the[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  **required** floor (document the CLI commands + the three agents) from[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  **nice-to-have** detail, so a minimal-but-correct README can be judged as[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  passing.[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  [m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  ## Risky steps[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  [m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  - **Editing the artifact-naming example requires care**:[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  `3-fix.md`→`5-fix.md` etc. must match `artifactPath` numbering exactly, or[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  the "verification" checklist will propagate a new inaccuracy.[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  - **Re-running the full integrity suite is fine** (`gofmt -l .` clean, `go[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  vet ./...` clean, `go test ./...` passes in ~2.2s — verified), but note[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  `TestInteractiveStageEndsLingeringAgent` launches a stand-in `sleep 3600` on[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  a PATH stub; do not weaken/alter it while documenting.[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  - **Do not "fix" the uncommitted Go work** to make a clean `git diff` — that[m[K
[1;38;2;25;103;210m  directly violates the task constraint.[m[K
